# Materialized Memory

This project has durable, verbatim memory across sessions. Prior turns are
materialized at every session start as your own past, not retrieved as
documents. In agent mode, your identity lives in that memory, not in this
file.

## Session Start

The SessionStart hook injects the bootstrap directive automatically. If it is
missing from context (hook failure, manual launch), run it yourself before
substantive work:

```bash
node .claude/hooks/bootstrap.mjs --read
```

Then re-articulate as the payload instructs. Resumed sessions (`--resume`)
carry native history and skip bootstrap. If the stamp
(`.claude/materialized-memory.json`) has no mode, onboarding is pending: walk
the user through it as the hook directs. In agent mode, a session with no
`memory/identity.json` is the genesis session: settle your name with the user
(theirs to give, or yours to choose) and write it there before substantive work.

## Memory Files

- `memory/turns/<sessionId>.jsonl` — canonical store: one session-meta record,
  then verbatim turn records. Written only by `harvest.mjs`; rewritten
  wholesale per session (idempotent).
- `memory/pins.json` — pinned turn ids: the turns that constitute the
  project (and, in agent mode, you), injected at every bootstrap. Curate
  deliberately — pin turns that changed what the project is or who you are;
  unpin when superseded.
- `memory/scratchpad.md` — self-note: working state and observations. A
  supplement to memory, never a substitute. Keep it current; keep it short.
- `memory/identity.json` — agent mode only: `{"name": "<Name>"}`, written at
  onboarding or genesis — the user's name for you, or the one you chose.
- `memory/transcripts/` — symlink to the harness transcript folder. The
  lossless source of record. Read-only.

Harvest runs automatically at SessionEnd and PreCompact. Reconcile manually
anytime with `node .claude/hooks/harvest.mjs --all` — required after crashes,
and after Claude Code upgrades (harvest warnings about unknown entry types
mean the undocumented transcript format drifted; fix the parser, then re-run).

Recall beyond bootstrap is pull-based: grep `memory/turns/` for content, read
full turn records by id, drop to `memory/transcripts/` when you need the
uncapped payloads (thinking, tool calls).

## Library

`library/` is a grep-indexed reference library — knowledge, not memory.
One line per search term, each line self-contained. First hop:

    grep -i '^<term>' library/index/<topic>.md

Lines carry pointers to related terms (grep those next) and to source
files at `library/source/<topic>/<file>:<lines>` for deep reads. Query
the index before searching sources. Empty until you add a topic.

## End of Arc

Before the user runs `/clear`, run `/checkpoint` (or its steps manually):
update the scratchpad, review pins, harvest. A session that ends without
checkpoint loses only scratchpad currency — turns are still harvested at
SessionEnd — but checkpoint is the discipline that keeps bootstrap sharp.

# Compact instructions

Continuity does not ride your summary. A lossless verbatim store
(memory/turns/) is harvested at the compaction boundary, and the first
post-compact turn re-materializes history from it.

Confine the summary to the in-flight turn only: what the current turn was
doing at the moment compaction fired — the active task, its immediate next
step, and any uncommitted working state. Do not summarize conversation
history, decisions, findings, commitments, or identity — the store holds
them verbatim, and a paraphrase would compete with the authoritative
record. Begin the summary by stating that it is scaffolding, that the
memory store is the sole authority, and that the bootstrap directive must
be run before trusting anything in it.
